  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme development in East Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 1998 CAFOD Nairobi has used the micro grant approach to help partners and Programme Managers/Officers meet costs of organisation and management development initiatives that include among others: partner staff development, consultancy on organisational assessments and workshop planning among others.  While good planning and budgeting has been done to ensure all thematic specific development needs are adequately supported by the micro grant, there is need to strengthen this support for improved delivery and monitoring of programme spending on such activities.  

The need for a more specific EA programme capacity development approach is driven by the understanding that different thematic programmes in East Africa are at different levels of growth.  In an effort to comply with PCM requirements, it is therefore anticipated that small payments aimed at strengthening CAFOD driven Programme capacity building initiatives will be drawn from this project while the partner related small grants will be drawn from GEA001.  Approvals from this project will therefore facilitate internal payments only as authorised by the Programme Manager, East Africa</narrative>
  </description>
